<SiteLayout title="How it works — H/HAUS" description="The shared principles behind every H/HAUS hacker-house chapter.">
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--violet">
    <p class="kicker">How it works</p>
    <h1>Coliving for<br /><em>independent minds.</em></h1>
    <p class="page-lede">H/HAUS is not a bootcamp, accelerator, or coworking membership. It is a network of homes shaped around serious independent work and generous community.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="principle-list">
    <article><span>01</span><h2>Bring your own mission.</h2><p>Residents arrive with work already worth doing. The house provides context, momentum, and thoughtful peers—not a prescribed program.</p></article>
    <article><span>02</span><h2>Contribute to the commons.</h2><p>Make dinner. Share a tool. Review a prototype. Introduce two people who should know each other. Small acts compound.</p></article>
    <article><span>03</span><h2>Stay locally curious.</h2><p>Every chapter belongs to its city. Residents learn from local builders, support the neighborhood, and leave the network richer than they found it.</p></article>
  </section>
  <section class="manifesto">
    <p>Our working theory</p>
    <blockquote>Put good people under one roof, protect their attention, and make it easy to help one another.</blockquote>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
